cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PITCIC land cover segmentation"
message: "If you use this code, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Paim de Cerqueira Melo de Souza"
    given-names: "João Victor"
    affiliation: "Instituto Militar de Engenharia"
  - family-names: "Siviero Passos"
    given-names: "Luan"
    affiliation: "Instituto Militar de Engenharia"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction code for the land cover segmentation stage of PITCIC: a U-Net
  with an EfficientNetB0 encoder trained on DeepGlobe at 2 m/px and adapted to
  CBERS-4A WPM imagery over the Brazilian Pampa with 100 hand-annotated tiles.
  Output is a six-class land cover raster built to feed an existing terrain
  traversability estimator as its land cover layer.
keywords:
  - semantic segmentation
  - remote sensing
  - land cover
  - CBERS-4A
  - terrain traversability
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jvpcms/pitcic-segmentation"
